    },
    "message": "feat(admin): turn Get Started into a step-by-step walkthrough\n\nThe checklist shipped in 4.29.0 said what to do but not how, and its button\ndropped you at the top of a long page with no indication of which control it\nmeant. \"Connect a model provider\" -> Providers, then hunt.\n\nThree changes.\n\nEach step now carries an ordered list of concrete instructions -- the real\nclick path, naming the real controls. Every label cited was checked against\nindex.html rather than written from memory: the footer button is literally\n\"Apply\", and the nav entries are \"Providers\" and \"Model Config\". A wrong\nlabel in a walkthrough costs a reader more than a wrong label anywhere else,\nbecause they will look for the thing you named and conclude the app is\nbroken when it is not there.\n\nEach step also carries an optional DOM target, so the button scrolls to and\nbriefly highlights the specific card or field instead of the page top --\n`#providerGrid`, `[data-key=\"MODEL\"]`, `#claudeSettingsPanel` and so on. Every\nselector was confirmed present before being wired.\n\nThe list now reads as a walkthrough rather than a wall: the first incomplete\nrequired step is expanded with its instructions visible, everything else\ncollapses to one line. It also advances -- once the expanded step becomes\ndone, the next incomplete required step takes its place, so finishing a step\nalways leaves the next action on screen. That was the first version's real\ndefect: the expanded id was chosen once and never re-derived, so completing\nthe provider step left it expanded and showing \"Done\" while the next action\nsat collapsed out of sight.\n\nWhich step is expanded is view state and is deliberately NOT persisted. The\nonly two things this feature stores remain `dismissed` and the guide's\n`visited` list; everything else is still derived from live configuration.\n\nVerification, against a live server on a throwaway HOME:\n\n    GET /admin/api/onboarding\n    required 0/3  complete=False\n      provider    target='#providerGrid'                  instructions=4\n      models      target='[data-key=\"MODEL\"]'             instructions=3\n      client      target='#claudeSettingsPanel'           instructions=3\n      websearch   target='[data-key=\"WEB_SEARCH_PROVIDER\"]' instructions=4\n      messaging   target='[data-key=\"MESSAGING_PLATFORM\"]'  instructions=4\n      analytics   target='#reqStatsCards'                 instructions=3\n      guide       target=None                             instructions=1\n\nA brand-new install reporting 0 of 3 is the assertion worth having; the one\nstep showing done there is web search, because a real EXA_API_KEY is present\nin this shell's environment and `load_value_state` reads `os.environ` -- the\nsame known local artifact behind 8 of the 14 baseline test failures, not a\ndefect.\n\nAlso: ruff format, ruff check, ty check clean; node --check on admin.js;\ntests/config tests/api tests/contracts 1061 passed on the rebased base.\n\nNot verified: the collapse/expand interaction and the scroll-and-highlight\nhave not been driven in a browser. The state machine is covered by reading\nit and the payload above is real, but the animation and highlight are not.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
